        d['evidence']['interpretation']='NCCP cites small phase I/II studies of weekly cisplatin with accelerated or concomitant-boost radiation. These radiation schedules and delivered dose counts differ from a general six-week course. JCOG1008 provides separate postoperative evidence; it does not establish equivalence for every unresectable definitive-radiation patient. No comparative survival benefit is assigned to this particular six-dose plan.'
        cp['evidence_at_a_glance']['trial']='NCCP-cited Beckmann 2005 and Medina 2006 phase I/II studies; separate postoperative JCOG1008 evidence'
        cp['evidence_at_a_glance']['qualitative_result']='Weekly 40 mg/m² is source-authorised in the stated cisplatin-tolerability context. The small uncontrolled radiation studies do not quantify comparative benefit for this exact six-dose pathway.'
